    {
      "type": "Block",
      "value": "---\nesid: sec-Intl.Locale.prototype.getCollations\ndescription: >\n  Language subtags with more than three letters are supported.\ninfo: |\n  CollationsOfLocale ( loc )\n  1. If loc.[[Collation]] is not undefined, then\n    a. Return CreateArrayFromList(« loc.[[Collation]] »).\n  2. Let _match_ be LookupMatchingLocaleByPrefix(%Intl.Collator%.[[AvailableLocales]], « _loc_.[[Locale]] »).\n  3. If _match_ is not *undefined*, then\n    ...\n  4. Else,\n    1. Let _list_ be « *\"emoji\"*, *\"eor\"* ».\n  5. Let _sorted_ be a copy of _list_, sorted according to lexicographic code unit order.\n  6. Return CreateArrayFromList(sorted).\nfeatures: [Intl.Locale, Intl.Locale-info]\n---",
      "start": 126,
      "end": 793
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " \"abcdefgh\" is not a registered language, so it always returns the default",
      "start": 795,
      "end": 871
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " locale's collations.",
      "start": 872,
      "end": 895
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " Except if an explicit \"co\" Unicode extension subtag is present.",
      "start": 1015,
      "end": 1081
    }
